.TH "SPGEN-EVENT" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-event \- Generates an event module and its test describe block
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.event [options] <EVENT>
.SH DESCRIPTION
A fact that happened. Events are the unit of behaviour that the aggregate, the projector and their tests are written against.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the event and its data.
.SH "What the generator does"
use TypedStruct, use ExConstructor, @derive Jason.Encoder, and the payload by what the event does (derived from the read model's projection rule, so \-\-template is usually omitted):
.IP \[bu] 2
create — every required field, enforce: true per field.
.IP \[bu] 2
update — id enforced, payload optional, plus get_changes/1, which returns only the non\-nil changed fields without the id. That function is the projector's partial\-update source.
.IP \[bu] 2
delete — id only.
.PP
Never enforce: true at struct level: optional fields have to stay omittable.
.SH Tests
The event owns the event test (./event\-test.md): describe "Event" with the construction, enforced\-field and JSON serialization cases. The get_changes/1 semantics are still manual (Known gaps (../../README.md#known\-gaps)).
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/events/<_event>.ex (typedstruct fact with enforces)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/events/<_event>_test.exs (construction and serialization tests)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
what the operation does: create|update|delete|none (optional: the model declares the operation for this element)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
create
.IP \(bu 2
update
.IP \(bu 2
delete
.IP \(bu 2
none
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIEVENT\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: operation, feature
